<description>&lt;p&gt;Militant groups and bandits continue to attack civilians in northern Nigeria, forcing tens of thousands to flee into Niger and prompting rescue operations for kidnapped victims in Niger and Adamawa. In Chad, jihadist fighters killed 23 soldiers, including a company commander, while fighting over the Tibesti gold mines. Mali’s forces recaptured Kidal using Russian electronic-warfare vehicles and Africa Corps drones are conducting lethal strikes there, as rival terror groups devastate the Sahel. The EU has summoned diplomats over Algerian and Russian troop deployments in Niger, and Mer Group secured a €46 million West African intelligence and cyber contract. 4,159 battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiW0FVX3lxTE9nbXFMQ3VGb1NoQmhSRlh0dUdpU1ZGVm44MVRxZFNGODFuVmp1RjRGR2hLYzZnUWpUWWpoV0RieWpCZ0lYVXJwR1ZMTlgtOThMdmVTcUhveElmcEk?oc=5&quot;&gt;BBC&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiqwFBVV95cUxOb2xYNnBaTFZmOEc1UFZvR0tnV2RHUnJ2WGNCZ3VqU2VBMzNOaEktZjhUcF9XNlNaNDIydk9ZbU5zQnJhSGdhQ05ib1dHME50Qm9HeGhTWHJHYXpacm45QlZMaE5XVmF1LUJld3NIWnJwOEhKclNrOENTQTN0TDBXLWFrSzQ0RXM1cVhiWnprQ1hzNHVCLWhxN05OaG5vRW14ODhYVTZ4MDlVOWM?oc=5&quot;&gt;Reuters&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMivAFBVV95cUxPWGxacGNiYVd5UnI3YVU1NnEwcVJKdExkNE1SelhmZHUwaEhpNDBTemVaNGtMRkNmWk5SV2ZYZTZxSjhFS0d5NjVYOFFpeVd6T2drMFVEejYtMEQ1NjJjSmhESE4zaW14U0ZXa1ZMMndhNmtFajRMX09zQ2w4ZFlYdXlvTUtQTktEWXpYQnRHNlMxX2g0OVNMRks0eVlOa0llSnQ1TTAxcFItY2xkdXpKRWkycG9lNzhMRDRUeQ?oc=5&quot;&gt;ZAgazola&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;The Nation Newspaper&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMinAFBVV95cUxPUkNYVnRJWnR2N2NXaUpSMnlId2pDWk1nTV93UndWYU1lQ1czVVh0NXpIYllSdU9ZaVg3eXRUOVIyLURZR